    {
        n = get_int("What's n? ");
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        printf("meow\n");
    }
}
```
Notice that this may stop the user from typing a number less than zero once. But what happens if they do it multiple times?
- Improve your code as follows:
```
// Uses a loop with continue/break.

#include <cs50.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    int n;
